AGP's policy gate, signed journal, and nonce-HITL relay derive their design and
semantics from CCSC's Apache-2.0 source (see the "Adapted from CCSC ..."
provenance headers in src/), reimplemented under AGP's own typed contracts and
hardened beyond the reference. As an Apache-2.0 derivative the attribution above
is retained. The upstream commit pin (CCSC v0.10.0 / 023cab3) and the
drift-review process are recorded in substrate/UPSTREAM.md. Per ADR
000-docs/040-AT-ADR-substrate-boundary-reconciliation-2026-06-12.md, AGP consumes
CCSC by reimplementation ("adapt-and-harden") at v0; the earlier vendor decision
(009-AT-ADR Option A) is superseded for v0, with the shared-package end-state
(009 Option D) retained, trigger-gated on a second consumer.
